---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Roomwave keeps about presenters and audiences, why, for how long, and how to have it deleted." path="/privacy">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="What we keep, and why." lead="Last updated 15 October 2026." />
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>If you answer in a session</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need an account and we do not ask who you are. Your phone gets a random identifier for that session, kept in your browser, so that you are counted once and can
        reconnect. We keep your answers, any question you send, and any name you choose to add. The presenter sees them, and may download them.
      </p>
      <p>Answers are anonymous unless you add a name. Quiz nicknames are made up for you and can be changed.</p>

      <h2>If you present</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your name, your email address and your password (stored only as a one-way hash), the presentations you make, and the answers given in your sessions. We use your
        email to sign you in, to reset your password and to send the reports you ask for. We do not send marketing email.
      </p>
      <p>If you try Roomwave without an account, your guest workspace and everything in it is deleted after a day unless you save it as an account.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p>
        We use one cookie, to keep you signed in. Phones that join a session keep a small identifier in the browser. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies, and there are no
        third-party analytics on Roomwave.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> carries traffic to our servers and protects them from attacks.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers the emails you ask for: password links and reports.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We never sell data, and we do not share it with anyone else unless the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Presentations and session results: until you delete them or your account.</li>
        <li>Guest workspaces: one day.</li>
        <li>PDF reports: kept for 14 days, then drawn again when you next ask for one.</li>
        <li>Password links: one hour, used once.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your details or delete your account from <strong>Account</strong> at any time. Deleting your account deletes your presentations and every session's results
        straight away. To ask about your data, write to us from the <a href="/contact?topic=support">contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>We handle personal data in line with Kenya's Data Protection Act, 2019.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
